# Story 3.14: org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor is loaded via this classic SPI
# file (SpringFactoriesLoader.forDefaultResourceLocation(), reading META-INF/spring.factories),
# NOT via a META-INF/spring/<FQCN>.imports file — verified against the actual pinned Spring Boot
# version (4.1.x) by decompiling EnvironmentPostProcessorsFactory.fromSpringFactories() and
# SpringFactoriesLoader, since the org.springframework.boot.env.EnvironmentPostProcessor.imports
# convention (the newer, `.env`-package interface) does not apply to this
# org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor (the current, non-deprecated one) on this
# version. This is a different, earlier-executing SPI than
# META-INF/spring/org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.AutoConfiguration.imports (read only
# during ApplicationContext refresh) — SpringApplication reads this one before any
# ApplicationContext exists.
org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
br.com.sawcunhaos.foundation.jdempotent.redis.configuration.ScosJdempotentRedisEnvironmentPostProcessor
